 ## Operating characteristics
 **Time and Memory Complexity:**
-*   **Space:** Reduces space complexity from $O(n^3)$ (for a dense grid of resolution $n$) to $O(n \cdot R)$ or $O(n)$ if $R$ is considered constant relative to $n$ [S2][S4][S6, unofficial]. For a 300x300x300 grid with $P=27$ channels, CP with $R=192$ uses 360K parameters, achieving a 0.048% compression rate compared to 756M parameters in a dense grid [S2].
-*   **Time:** Reconstruction quality improves with more iterations, but higher $R$ increases training time [S2]. TensoRF with CP achieves reconstruction in less than 30 minutes with a model size < 4MB [S6, unofficial].
+*   **Space:** Reduces space complexity from $O(n^3)$ (for a dense grid of resolution $n$) to $O(n \cdot R)$ or $O(n)$ if $R$ is considered constant relative to $n$ [S2][S4, unofficial][S6, unofficial]. For a 300x300x300 grid with $P=27$ channels, CP with $R=192$ uses 360K parameters, achieving a 0.048% compression rate compared to 756M parameters in a dense grid [S2].
+*   **Time:** Reconstruction quality improves with more iterations, but higher $R$ increases training time [S2]. TensoRF with CP achieves reconstruction in less than 30 minutes with a model size < 4MB [S5][S7, unofficial].
 
